 Adding, renaming and tagging reject bad input with an `invalid-input` error and leave the list unchanged:
 a title that is empty, blank or over 120 characters; a priority other than `low`, `normal` or `high`; a
 tag that is empty or contains a space.
+
+## Bulk import
+
+`importTasks(list, text)` adds tasks from text with one task per line, as `title;priority;tags`, for
+example `Renew the insurance;high;admin money`. The priority may be empty for a normal one, and tags are
+separated by spaces. Blank lines are skipped. It returns `{ imported, rejected }`: how many tasks were
+added, and each line that could not be added as `{ line, reason }`, with `line` counting from 1 (blank
+lines count). A line is rejected for the same reasons as `add` (bad title, priority or tag, or a title
+already in the list) or for having more than three fields; the other lines are still imported.
